.TH CHIMP 1 "2026-11" "chimp 0.8.0"
.SH NAME
chimp \- MIDI controllers as a KDE Plasma control deck (editor)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimp
.RB [ \-\-program
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B chimp
.BR \-\-version " | " \-\-check\-install
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimp
is the editor for Chimp. It reads and writes the four programs of an Akai
LPD8 mk2 (pads, knobs, colours, channels) over SysEx, learns the controls of
any other MIDI controller, and assigns desktop actions to each control:
volume of the system, the focused app, a playing app or the running game,
microphone, brightness, media keys, shortcuts, apps, commands and OBS scenes.
.PP
The actions are carried out by
.BR chimpd (1),
which runs as the systemd user service
.BR chimp.service .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-program " N"
Open on LPD8 program tab
.I N
(1\(en4).
.TP
.BI \-\-device " NAME"
Open on the MIDI device whose name contains
.IR NAME .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-install
Import every module and compile every QML file offscreen, then exit: 0 if
everything loads, 1 with the errors otherwise. Needs no display or device.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/chimp/
Desktop actions, device profiles and overlay settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/chimp/controllers/
Your own controller files (YAML): what a controller's pads, knobs, faders and buttons
send, so it can be set up without Learn. The format is in the README.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chimpd (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
